---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { href } from '../lib/utils';

/**
 * To change the photo, replace public/about-portrait.jpg and update the
 * width/height below to match the new file. It's shown blurred on purpose.
 */
const portrait = href('/about-portrait.jpg');
const repo = `${site.social.github}/blog`;
const mailto = `mailto:${site.email}`;
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={site.description}>
  <div class="about">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

    <div class="about__grid">
      <figure class="portrait">
        <span class="portrait__frame">
          <img
            class="portrait__img"
            src={portrait}
            width="320"
            height="640"
            alt="Portrait of Sobhan, deliberately obscured"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <span class="portrait__grain" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </span>
      </figure>

      <div class="about__text">
        <h2 class="about__h">About me</h2>
        <p class="about__lead">
          I have a passion for computer games and for being out in nature,
          especially when it is dark and cold (a huge plus if it is snowing).
        </p>

        <p>
          I work as an Observability Engineer, and I have a really, and I mean
          really, strong interest in cybersecurity, particularly malware
          research labs.
        </p>

        <p>
          In short, I'm just a normal, chill dude who happens to be extremely
          competitive.
        </p>

        <h2 class="about__h">About this website</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>No tracking.</strong> There is not a single analytics tool or
          tracker on this website. It sets no cookies and collects nothing, so
          I have no idea how many people visit, who they are, or when they came.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>No generative AI.</strong> I use AI every day: for work,
          research, learning, building tools, and even for fun. But I am
          strongly against using it for communication between people, so I
          think it is worth saying plainly: every word here is written by me,
          in my own words. AI helped build the website itself; it did not write
          the content. If you are reading something here, you are reading my
          thoughts, my opinions and my words, not AI-generated text.
        </p>

        <h2 class="about__h">How is this website made?</h2>
        <p>
          I write everything in Markdown and keep it in a small
          <a href={repo} rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository</a>.
          <a href="https://astro.build" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>
          turns that Markdown into HTML, so every page is a plain static file
          with nothing running behind it.
        </p>

        <p>
          If that sounds technical, it is simpler than it sounds. Building a
          website is within reach for anyone, and having your own corner of the
          Internet gives you far more control over what you share than social
          media platforms do, where everything you make lives inside someone
          else's ecosystem and is practically owned by them.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you want to set up your own site and need a hand, take a look at
          the <a href={repo} rel="noopener noreferrer">repository</a>, and if
          you have any questions, <a href={mailto}>let me know</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="about__h">Elsewhere</h2>
        <p class="about__links">
          <a href={site.social.github} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
          <a href={site.social.telegram} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Telegram</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
          <a href={site.social.linkedin} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
